  "prefLabel": "Env-A 103.22 Federal implementation plan",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 103.22 “Federal implementation plan” means “federal implementation plan” as defined in section 302(y) of the Act, namely “a plan (or portion thereof) promulgated by the Administrator to fill all or a portion of a gap or otherwise correct all or a portion of an inadequacy in a State implementation plan, and which includes enforceable emission limitations or other control measures, means or techniques (including economic incentives, such as marketable permits or auctions of emissions allowances), and provides for attainment of the relevant national ambient air quality standard.”\n\nSource. #6057-A, eff 6-30-95; renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.122), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.78), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.78) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a100.html"
